WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.840
Today, we're going to talk about how NOT
to prepare for law school. So stick

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.200
around and get a head start.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.960
Here at Legal Eagle, we've talked a lot about

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.550
what you should do before you start law
school so you can get a head start and a

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:21.090
leg up on your classmates, which is
really important because you're going to

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:25.710
be graded on a curve, so every advantage
you can get is important. But there's a

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.310
lot of bad information out there and
there's a lot of mistakes you can make

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:33.809
before starting law school. Here are some
of the worst things that you can do

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:39.480
before starting law school. So the first
thing you should not do before starting

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:45.809
law school is you should not read your
case book. This is a case book it's a

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:50.489
compilation of all the cases that you're
going to read in your class. Now the last

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:54.660
thing that you should do is start
opening it up and reading inside.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:59.460
Number one, you're not going to cover everything
that's in the book. Number two, every

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:03.960
professor is different, so even different
professors would use the same case in

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.590
different ways, and you're going to have
to learn how your particular professor

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:12.990
uses that case book. Now on top of that,
if you did start reading it, a lot of the

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:17.490
cases wouldn't make a lot of sense.
That's because the law needs to be

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:22.650
interpreted. Sometimes you use the facts
from a certain case as a point of

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:26.250
reference. Sometimes you only use
bright-line rules, and you ignore the

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:30.390
facts, and it's up to your professor to
tell you what's important to take away

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:35.670
from every particular case. In addition,
it's really complicated stuff, and there

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:40.740
are hundreds of books that are out there
to help digest that material. Books like

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.880
commercial supplements and commercial
outlines, so digging into your case book

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.899
while it might seem like a good idea and
a good way to get ahead is actually a

00:01:48.899 --> 00:01:53.340
terrible idea. It's just going to create
more stress. And speaking of commercial

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:58.259
don't read those either. Here's
a commercial outline from Gilbert's

00:01:58.259 --> 00:02:03.509
on torts. A commercial outline contains a
summary of a particular subject, in this

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:10.229
case torts. But it's a bad idea to sit
down and read those too - first of all, it's

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:16.159
hundreds of pages long and these are big pages. It would be a huge task to

00:02:16.159 --> 00:02:20.510
try and read through it, and you have at
least three substantive courses every

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:23.659
semester. You're not going to get through
it, and even if you did you probably

00:02:23.659 --> 00:02:28.609
wouldn't really understand it, even in its
broken down components. And again you

00:02:28.609 --> 00:02:33.290
have to understand the law as your
professor presents it to you. Your

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:36.170
professor is the one that's going to be
giving you a final exam, and that

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:41.419
professor is going to write their final
by themselves. So it's really important

00:02:41.419 --> 00:02:45.500
to understand the law as your professor
gives it to you. Now,

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:50.810
we love commercial outlines and
supplements at Legal Eagle, they play a very

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:55.669
vital role when you're studying for
class. But the summer before law school

00:02:55.669 --> 00:03:00.230
starts is not the right time to read it.
It's a recipe for disaster, it's just not

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:05.090
worth it. Which leads me to my third
point: don't try understanding the law

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:10.340
before you get to law school. It would
take an incredibly long time. Lawyers

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.930
spend their entire careers learning very
small portions of the law. And any

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:19.489
advantage you would have in learning the
substantive law would quickly be erased

00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:23.720
as people started boning up themselves
on the law itself. Which leads me to my

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:28.669
next point: don't freak out. Law School is
a very stressful time no doubt about it.

00:03:28.669 --> 00:03:32.810
But it's also wonderful.
You'll meet great people, you will

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:36.500
stretch yourself academically in ways
that you didn't think you were capable

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.870
of. You will learn things that you had no
idea existed. Every day you're going to

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:46.609
learn something new, and if you play your
cards right in law school you're going

00:03:46.609 --> 00:03:50.209
to have a great time and it's going to
be worthwhile. I can tell you as a

00:03:50.209 --> 00:03:54.019
practicing trial attorney it was an
incredibly worthwhile experience and I

00:03:54.019 --> 00:03:59.060
would do it again if I had to. Which
brings me to my final tip: don't do

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:04.370
nothing. Now sure it's tempting to just
sit back on a beach and relax before you

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:08.479
start law school, but now is the time
where you really can get a head start.

00:04:08.479 --> 00:04:13.129
And you get a head start not by studying
the law, but by studying law school

00:04:13.129 --> 00:04:17.900
itself. So many people go into law school
not knowing anything about the process

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:22.159
itself, and specifically they don't know
anything about how to take law school

00:04:22.159 --> 00:04:25.670
exams, but law school exams are kind of
like the LSATs.

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:29.900
There are strategies and there are
tactics to do better, and you can

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:35.900
practice those tactics ahead of time. In
our video on the two pillars of law

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:41.270
school success, we talked about how you
have to both master the law and master

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:44.930
the tests in law school.
Everybody masters the law in law school

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:50.630
but so few people put in the time to
learn how to take law school exams well.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:56.750
And when your entire grade is based on
one single exam, it's so important to

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:01.910
learn how to do that exam. So while it's
tempting to just sit back, don't do

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:05.660
nothing before you start law school. So
there you go. Those are the things you

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:09.680
should not do before starting law school.
Hopefully that helps before you begin.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:14.510
You'll have a great time, it's definitely
worth it, and from everyone here at Legal

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:18.500
Eagle, remember to study smart through
law school.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.600
Oh and one last thing,

